> Here’s a ready-to-run outline you can drop straight into play. I’ll keep rules light and always give you simple “present this choice / ask for this roll” instructions.
> 
> I’ll assume:
> - Ekemon: tiefling fighter 2 with Titan Seed, Varkash: dragonborn fighter-ish, Dru/Johanna: wood elf druid.
> - You can fudge DCs on the fly. I’ll suggest ballparks.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## SCENE 1 – Road to the Canyon: Omens & Bonding
> 
> **Goal:** Mood, choices, small stakes, grow the politics & Titan theme.
> 
> ### 1.1 Opening Travel & Titan Vibes
> 
> Describe:
> - Narrow path through rocky hills, wind constantly shifting around Ekemon.
> - Distant low rumbles of thunder, even though the sky is mostly clear.
> - The Titan Seed beats like a heart when lightning flashes on the horizon.
> 
> **Quick RP Prompt:**
> - Ask each: “What does your character talk about on the road?”
>   - Dru: explain the Fourfold Mother and the Storm-Titan myth.
>   - Varkash: maybe talks about glory, contracts, or distrust of priests.
>   - Ekemon: you ask your son what Ekemon wants from the Titan power.
> 
> > Optional check:  
> > - **DC 10 Insight (Dru or Varkash)** – Notice Ekemon seems more “stormy” when angry or excited.  
> > - On success, you can say: “You notice the wind and distant thunder seem to react to him.”
> 
> ---
> 
> ### 1.2 The Scorched Clearing
> 
> You crest a hill and see:
> - A big circle of blackened earth, charred stumps, and cracked soil.
> - A faint smell of ozone, like after lightning.
> - Maybe one living sapling in the middle, with a single green leaf.
> 
> **Choice moment:**
> Ask Ekemon, “What do you do?”
> 
> Possible actions & checks:
> 
> 1. **Investigate the Burn**
>    - **DC 10 Investigation or Nature (anyone)**  
>      - Success:  
>        - It’s older than a few days, but not _too_ old.  
>        - Lightning hit multiple times in a pattern, not a normal storm.
>      - Extra clue if you want: “It feels like something powerful _called_ the lightning.”
>    - **If Ekemon touches the ground:**  
>      - The Titan Seed thumps; tiny sparks dance on his fingers.
> 
> 2. **Heal / Bless the Sapling (Dru)**
>    - **DC 10 Nature or Survival** or a small druid spell (like Druidcraft flavor).  
>    - On success:  
>      - Sapling glows softly, a small breeze circles it, a hint of rain smell.
>      - Dru explains: “The land’s hurt. The Heartshard’s storms are lashing out.”
> 
> 3. **Ekemon’s Moral Mini-Choice**
>    - If he acts “mean”: like stomping a burned log, kicking ash  
>      → The sky rumbles approvingly; a gust of wind whips his cloak.
>    - If he acts “protective”: helps the sapling, promises to stop the storms  
>      → A cool, gentle breeze instead; softer thunder, like thanks.
> 
> You can narrate the storm “reacting” to his mood. No mechanics needed.
> 
> ---
> 
> ### 1.3 Farmers Arguing: Human God vs Druids
> 
> You come around a bend and see:
> - 2–3 farm wagons stopped on the road.
> - A group of **Farmers** arguing with a **Traveling Human Priest** (kind, not zealot).
> - One farmer: “The druids kept the river flowing for generations!”
> - Another: “The Human God’s knights protected us from raiders. We need them!”
> 
> When the party approaches, everyone goes quiet.
> 
> **Priest’s attitude:**
> - Recognizes Dru as a druid, Varkash as “a warrior”, and is wary of Ekemon’s horns.
> - Tries to be polite: “We all seek safety from these storms…”
> 
> **Choice: Who does Ekemon side with?**
> 1. **Support Druids** (“Nature and the four gods are important.”)
> 2. **Support Human Church** (“Order and protection are important.”)
> 3. **Try to be Neutral / Peacemaker** (“You both help in different ways…”)
> 
> Give a simple **DC 10 Persuasion** (or Intimidation if he goes that way).
> 
> - **On success** (for any side):  
>   - The crowd relaxes; that side likes them more.
>   - You can grant a small future bonus:
>     - “When you later talk to that faction, you’ll have advantage on one social roll.”
> - **On failure:**  
>   - They’re confused or still arguing, but no fight.
>   - Maybe:
>     - A farmer mutters: “Tieflings… Storms… This is all wrong.”
> 
> Optional Titan flavor:
> - When Ekemon **takes a strong stance**, the wind picks up again.
> - If he **tries to calm everyone**, the clouds thin and sun breaks through.
> 
> ---
> 
> ### 1.4 Weird Weather Follows Them
> 
> As they leave the farmers:
> 
> - A little **rain cloud** starts following Ekemon only.
>   - Rains in a 10-foot circle over him, nowhere else.
>   - Or: a ribbon of wind snakes around him, tugging at his whip or trident.
> 
> Let Ekemon choose how to react:
> - If he laughs and plays with it → the cloud copies him (tiny rainbow, fun).  
> - If he gets mad and yells → thunder crack, brief flash, but no damage.
> 
> **Optional check:**  
> - **DC 10 Arcana or Religion (Dru)** – “This isn’t normal magic. It’s Titan-stuff. The Heartshard is calling to you.”
> 
> Then transition: the canyon comes into view.
> 
> ---
> 
> ## SCENE 2 – First Look at the Canyon of Storms
> 
> ### 2.1 Describe the Canyon
> 
> Paint this clearly and simply:
> 
> - A huge **canyon** splits the land, with a roaring **river** at the bottom.
> - A **waterfall** crashes down from one side.
> - Halfway up the canyon wall: the partly-collapsed **Storm Temple**, built of pale stone, statues broken, one big central tower leaning.
> - Overhead: **dark storm clouds** circling in a big ring over the canyon, even though the sky behind you is blue.
> 
> Ask Ekemon:  
> - “How does he feel, seeing the place where the Titan Heartshard is?”
> 
> The Titan Seed:
> - Beats faster.
> - Maybe he hears a distant, slow heartbeat echoing from the canyon.
> 
> ---
> 
> ### 2.2 Factions’ Camps
> 
> Show them visually in your description:
> 
> **Druid Camp**
> - Tents and hammocks among cliffside trees on the **left** rim.
> - A few druids in green and brown, plus animal companions (owl, wolf, etc).
> - A big, older elf or half-elf: **Archdruid Lysara** (Dru’s mentor or respected elder).
> 
> **Human Church Camp**
> - On a rocky terrace on the **right** rim, closer to the main path down.
> - **Dawn-Knights** polishing armor, a few **priests** in white and gold.
> - A friendly-looking **Light-Priest Arlen**.
> - A tougher **Purifier Captain Marcen**, who remembers Ekemon from the Purifier fight.
> 
> Tell the player plainly:
> - “Neither side has reached the Heartshard yet. The inside of the temple is dangerous, with wild magic and storms.”
> - “Both sides are watching you. You can choose who you go talk to first.”
> 
> Ask: **Who do you go to first: the Druids’ camp or the Human Church camp?**
> 
> ---
> 
> ## SCENE 3 – The Druid Camp
> 
> (If they go here first. If not, run the Human camp scene first and swap the order.)
> 
> ### 3.1 Arrival & Welcome
> 
> - Dru is warmly welcomed.
> - Ekemon and Varkash get cautious looks, but no open hostility.
> 
> **Archdruid Lysara**:
> - Older elf, calm, hair with leaves braided in.
> - Speaks slowly and respectfully.
> 
> Key info to deliver (you can parcel it out in conversation):
> 
> - “The storm is the **Titan’s Heartshard** calling out from inside the old sky-temple.”
> - “We fear if it is **ripped out** or destroyed crudely, the canyon walls might collapse, or the weather across the region could go wild.”
> - “We want to **stabilize** it, soothe it, and maybe guide its power rather than smother it.”
> 
> **About Ekemon & the Titan Seed:**
> - Lysara steps closer, eyes narrowing kindly.
> - “You are already bound to a Titan’s echo. Perhaps you can **carry** this shard safely… or perhaps you are exactly the danger we fear.”
> 
> **Skill checks:**
> - **DC 10 Insight (Ekemon)** – Sense that she’s honestly worried, not manipulative.
> - **DC 10 Religion or Nature (Dru)** – Connect this to the Fourfold Mother:
>   - “The Fourfold Mother birthed the Titans like storm-children. They can protect or destroy, depending on how they are raised.”
> 
> You can let Ekemon ask:
> - “Will helping you make me more Titan, or less?”
>   - Answer: “We hope to make you a **guardian-Titan**, not a destroyer.”
> 
> ---
> 
> ### 3.2 Druid Request / Offer
> 
> They ask the party:
> 
> > “If you go into the temple, we ask that you **do not let the Heartshard be broken or stolen** for cruel purposes.”
> 
> Possible “quest conditions”:
> - If Ekemon agrees to “try to keep it whole” → they grant:
>   - A small **blessing of wind**: once in the temple, advantage on a single saving throw against lightning or falling.
> - If he refuses or is vague → they just look worried, but don’t attack.
> 
> You can state this clearly to your son:
> - “If you promise the druids you’ll protect the shard, you get one special bonus later. If you don’t, no bonus, but total freedom.”
> 
> ---
> 
> ## SCENE 4 – The Human Church Camp
> 
> ### 4.1 Arrival & Tension
> 
> - Camp is more formal, with banners and a small shrine.
> - **Light-Priest Arlen** steps forward with a peaceful gesture.
> - **Purifier Captain Marcen** hangs back, arms crossed, suspicious.
> 
> **Arlen** (kind tone):
> - “Welcome. You look like capable adventurers. The storms here are dangerous to everyone.”
> - “We believe this temple is a **den of false gods** and wild Titans. We must calm this storm for the safety of nearby villages.”
> 
> **Marcen** (rough tone):
> - Might say: “Tiefling. Druid. Dragonborn servant of some dragon cult? Hmph.”
> - He recognizes Ekemon from the earlier Purifier encounter, maybe mutters, “You again.”
> 
> **Skill checks:**
> - **DC 10 Persuasion (Ekemon)** – To get Arlen to overrule Marcen a bit:
>   - Success: Arlen says, “We judge by actions, not faces. Let’s hear them out.”
> - **DC 10 Intimidation** if Ekemon wants to posture as “dangerous Titan-champion”:
>   - Success: Marcen backs off a little, but now _really_ wants to keep an eye on him.
> 
> ---
> 
> ### 4.2 Human Church Perspective
> 
> Key info to deliver:
> 
> - “The storm is a **curse**, a sign that the Human God is displeased with old idol-worship.”
> - “We intend to **claim any powerful artifacts** inside, to keep them from wicked hands and use them for order and protection
